  "text": {
    "tagline": "joystick not included",
    "blurb": "chip leads, buzz basses and arcade arps for the sound recorder synths. made by static lagoon at 2am with a joystick still plugged into the game port.",
    "intro": [
      "game port sound set is our chiptune pack. every preset sounds like a cartridge left in the console too long: square leads, buzzing basses, little arpeggios, the bleep when you lose a life.",
      "mike built the arps by looping slices of the ding until they buzzed at the right pitch. veronica named every sound after a level we never finished."
    ],
    "maker_note": [
      "this is our second sound release, after the ansi packs and the music disks. call the board and leave a note in the game port message base.",
      "spread this disc. copy it for your friends. upload it to your board. do not sell it. if somebody sold you this, they owe you five dollars.",
      "-- pastelghost / sl"
    ],
    "install": [
      "put the disc in. open the library tab. the pack shows up as a cd drive called GAMEPORT_SL.",
      "double-click a preset in any folder to load it.",
      "no installer. no registry. no strings."
    ],
    "license": [
      "GAME PORT SOUND SET IS FREEWARE.",
      "you can copy this disc and give it away, upload it to any bbs, put it on a shareware cd. keep all the files together and do not change them.",
      "you can not sell it on its own. a cd-rom compilation can charge for the disc, not for our stuff.",
      "use the sounds in your own music, any way you like, no credit needed (credit is nice).",
      "there is no warranty. if your joystick drifts, it was already drifting."
    ],
    "greets": [
      "pastel riot",
      "the neon gutter bbs",
      "vhskids",
      "everyone on node 2 at 3am",
      "the security guard at the plaza who let us record the fountain",
      "cassette mike's mom, for the 486"
    ],
